<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14047" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĭo</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ōn</span></b> , ōnis, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δίων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A brother-in-law of the elder Dionysius, of
				Syracuse, the pupil and friend of Plato</i>. His life was
			written by Nepos and Plutarch; cf. also Cic Tusc. 5, 35;
					<i><span class="en">id. de Or. 3, 34</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Jornand. 2,
			92</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An Academic philosopher</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 4,
			12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A Stoic philosopher</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Leg. 3, 5
					<i>fin.</i></span></i> dub. (al.
			Diogenes).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			Dio Halaesinus, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 1, 10 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
